---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const SITE = 'https://dogtur.com';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Affiliate Disclosure | Dog Tur"
  description="How Dog Tur makes money: affiliate links on review and comparison pages, and why commissions never influence our rankings."
  canonical={`${SITE}/affiliate-disclosure/`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <h1>Affiliate disclosure</h1>
    <p>
      Dog Tur is reader-supported. Some links on this site — especially on
      review and comparison pages — are <strong>affiliate links</strong>. If
      you click one and make a purchase, we may earn a commission from the
      retailer <strong>at no extra cost to you</strong>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <em>As an Amazon Associate, Dogtur earns from qualifying purchases.</em>
    </p>
    <h2>What this means in practice</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Every page with affiliate links carries a disclosure box at the top.</li>
      <li>Commissions <strong>never influence rankings or verdicts</strong>. Product selections are currently based on research: published specifications, independent testing by other publications (always attributed), and analysis of verified owner reviews. We have <strong>not yet completed hands-on testing</strong> of our own — see <a href="/methodology/">our methodology</a> for exactly what goes into a review today.</li>
      <li>We recommend products we'd suggest to a friend with a senior dog, whether or not a link pays us.</li>
      <li>Affiliate programs we may participate in include (but aren't limited to) Amazon Associates and pet-retailer partner programs. Specific programs are named on the pages where they appear.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Why affiliate revenue</h2>
    <p>
      Running a review site costs money — hosting, research time, and
      eventually buying products retail to test them ourselves. Affiliate
      commissions are what make the site sustainable, and they are the reason
      we publish verdicts instead of selling sponsored placements. Hands-on
      testing is on our roadmap; when we complete it, we'll update our
      methodology and say so plainly.
    </p>
    <p><em>Last updated: September 2026.</em></p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
